{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cstdlib>\n#include <cstring>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <queue>\n#include <set>\n#include <stack>\n#include <map>\n#include <vector>\n#include <bitset>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\ntypedef unsigned long long ull;\n\nll scan() {\n    ll x = 0;\n    int c = getchar(), s = 1;\n    while (c < '0' || c > '9') {\n        if (c == '-') s = -1;\n        c = getchar();\n    }\n    x = c - '0';\n    while ((c = getchar()) >= '0' && c <= '9')\n        x = x * 10 + c - '0';\n    return x * s;\n}\n\nconst ll MOD = 1000000007;\n\nll mul_mod(ll a, ll b, ll mod) {\n    ll res = 0;\n    for (; b; b >>= 1) {\n        if (b & 1) res = (res + a) % mod;\n        a = (a + a) % mod;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nll pow_mod(ll base, ll exp, ll mod) {\n    ll res = 1;\n    for (; exp; exp >>= 1) {\n        if (exp & 1) res = mul_mod(res, base, mod);\n        base = mul_mod(base, base, mod);\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ll p = scan();\n    ll k = scan();\n    ll output;\n    if (k == 0) {\n        output = pow_mod(p, p - 1, MOD);\n    } else if (k == 1) {\n        output = pow_mod(p, p, MOD);\n    } else {\n        ll cnt = 1;\n        ll cur = k % MOD;\n        while (cur != 1) {\n            cur = (cur * k) % MOD;\n            ++cnt;\n        }\n        output = pow_mod(p, (p - 1) / cnt, MOD);\n    }\n    printf(\"%I64d\\n\", output);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 1000000007;\n\n    static long scan() throws IOException {\n        long x = 0;\n        int c = System.in.read();\n        int s = 1;\n        while (c < '0' || c > '9') {\n            if (c == '-') s = -1;\n            c = System.in.read();\n        }\n        x = c - '0';\n        while ((c = System.in.read()) >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n            x = x * 10 + c - '0';\n        }\n        return x * s;\n    }\n\n    static long mul_mod(long a, long b, long mod) {\n        long res = 0;\n        for (; b > 0; b >>= 1) {\n            if ((b & 1) == 1) {\n                res = (res + a) % mod;\n            }\n            a = (a + a) % mod;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    static long pow_mod(long base, long exp, long mod) {\n        long res = 1;\n        for (; exp > 0; exp >>= 1) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) {\n                res = mul_mod(res, base, mod);\n            }\n            base = mul_mod(base, base, mod);\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long p = scan();\n        long k = scan();\n        long output;\n        if (k == 0) {\n            output = pow_mod(p, p - 1, MOD);\n        } else if (k == 1) {\n            output = pow_mod(p, p, MOD);\n        } else {\n            long cnt = 1;\n            long cur = k % MOD;\n            while (cur != 1) {\n                cur = (cur * k) % MOD;\n                ++cnt;\n            }\n            output = pow_mod(p, (p - 1) / cnt, MOD);\n        }\n        System.out.println(output);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00015317220822907984, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00018010901112575084, -2.2411095415009186e-05, -0.1806100755929947, -0.47585228085517883, -8.83301836438477e-05, -1.7165990357170813e-05, -0.0014150853967294097, -0.0006735440110787749, -5.483612312673358e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.9907753085135482e-05, -0.003178308717906475, -0.00012385078298393637, -0.14295050501823425, -0.110085628926754, -0.00012051333033014089, -2.9802276912960224e-06, 0.0, -2.622600959512056e-06, 0.0, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -1.07287787614041e-05, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.022156324237585068, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0046304380521178246, -0.00022349244682118297, -0.0017864234978333116, -0.007220838218927383, -0.31334635615348816, -4.1960789531003684e-05, -3.313963316031732e-05, -1.1086402082582936e-05, -0.01627269946038723, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00015054999676067382, -9.775113539944869e-06, 0.0, -5.209310256759636e-05, -0.0001998939987970516, -1.0251946150674485e-05, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.001933254417963326, -2.038458114839159e-05, -1.2397689715726301e-05, -0.01815756969153881, -7.152555099310121e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -0.020549140870571136, -5.245195097813848e-06, -0.0007099968497641385, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.0005061537376604974, -0.00010966652916977182, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -6.198863957251888e-06, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, 